        "Azure.AI.Inference": {
          "name": "Azure AI Inference SDK",
          "content": "\n\n\n\n[The link to the NuGet package and some examples](https://aka.ms/azsdk/azure-ai-inference/csharp/package). For additional information about Azure AI Inference SDK, see full [documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/es-mx/samples/azure/azure-sdk-for-net/azureaiinference-samples/).\n\n\n## 1. Create a personal access token\n\n\nYou'll need to **[create a token](https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta)** to enable free API access.\n\nYou **do not need to give any permissions** to the token. Note that the token will be sent to a Microsoft service.\n\nTo use the code snippets below, create an environment variable to set your token as the key for the client code.\n\nIf you're using **bash**:\n\n```bash\nexport GITHUB_TOKEN=\"<your-github-token-goes-here>\"\n```\n\nIf you're in **powershell**:\n\n```powershell\n$Env:GITHUB_TOKEN=\"<your-github-token-goes-here>\"\n```\n\nIf you're using Windows command prompt:\n\n```\nset GITHUB_TOKEN=<your-github-token-goes-here>\n```\n\n\n\n## 2. Install dependencies\n\n1. Install [dotnet runtime](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/en-us/download/dotnet/)\n2. Open power shell at the desired project folder, restore the environment and run the program.\n\n```\ndotnet restore\ndotnet run\n```\n\n\n\n## 3. Run a basic code sample\n\nThis sample demonstrates a basic call to the chat completion API. It is leveraging the GitHub AI model inference endpoint and your GitHub token. The call is synchronous.\n\n```csharp\nusing Azure;\nusing Azure.AI.Inference;\n\n\nvar endpoint = new Uri(\"https://models.inference.ai.azure.com\");\nvar credential = new AzureKeyCredential(System.Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(\"GITHUB_TOKEN\"));\nvar model = \"meta-llama-3-8b-instruct\";\n\nvar client = new ChatCompletionsClient(\n    endpoint,\n    credential,\n    new ChatCompletionsClientOptions());\n\nvar requestOptions = new ChatCompletionsOptions()\n{\n    Messages =\n    {\n        new ChatRequestSystemMessage(\"You are a helpful assistant.\"),\n        new ChatRequestUserMessage(\"What is the capital of France?\"),\n    },\n    Model = model,\n    Temperature = 1,\n    MaxTokens = 1000,\n\n};\n\nResponse<ChatCompletions> response = client.Complete(requestOptions);\nSystem.Console.WriteLine(response.Value.Choices[0].Message.Content);\n```\n\n\n\n## 4. Explore more samples\n\n\n\n\n### Run a multi-turn conversation\n\nThis sample demonstrates a multi-turn conversation with the chat completion API. When using the model for a chat application, you'll need to manage the history of that conversation and send the latest messages to the model.\n\n```csharp\nusing Azure;\nusing Azure.AI.Inference;\n\n\nvar endpoint = new Uri(\"https://models.inference.ai.azure.com\");\nvar credential = new AzureKeyCredential(System.Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(\"GITHUB_TOKEN\"));\nvar model = \"meta-llama-3-8b-instruct\";\n\nvar client = new ChatCompletionsClient(\n    endpoint,\n    credential,\n    new ChatCompletionsClientOptions());\n\n// Create an initial request to the chatbot.\nvar requestOptions = new ChatCompletionsOptions()\n{\n    Messages =\n    {\n        new ChatRequestSystemMessage(\"You are a helpful assistant.\"),\n        new ChatRequestUserMessage(\"What is the capital of France?\"),\n    },\n    Model = model\n};\nResponse<ChatCompletions> response = client.Complete(requestOptions);\nSystem.Console.WriteLine(response.Value.Choices[0].Message.Content);\n// Append the model response to the chat history.\nrequestOptions.Messages.Add(new ChatRequestAssistantMessage(response.Value.Choices[0].Message));\n// Append new user question.\nrequestOptions.Messages.Add(new ChatRequestUserMessage(\"What about Spain?\"));\n\nresponse = client.Complete(requestOptions);\nSystem.Console.WriteLine(response.Value.Choices[0].Message.Content);\n```\n\n### Stream the output\n\nFor a better user experience, you will want to stream the response of the model so that the first token shows up early and you avoid waiting for long responses.\n\n```csharp\nusing Azure;\nusing Azure.AI.Inference;\n\n\nvar endpoint = new Uri(\"https://models.inference.ai.azure.com\");\nvar credential = new AzureKeyCredential(System.Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(\"GITHUB_TOKEN\"));\nvar model = \"meta-llama-3-8b-instruct\";\n\nvar client = new ChatCompletionsClient(\n    endpoint,\n    credential,\n    new ChatCompletionsClientOptions());\n\nvar requestOptions = new ChatCompletionsOptions()\n{\n    Messages =\n    {\n        new ChatRequestSystemMessage(\"You are a helpful assistant.\"),\n        new ChatRequestUserMessage(\"Give me 5 good reasons why I should exercise every day.\"),\n    },\n    Model = model\n};\n\nStreamingResponse<StreamingChatCompletionsUpdate> response = await client.CompleteStreamingAsync(requestOptions);\nawait foreach (StreamingChatCompletionsUpdate chatUpdate in response)\n{\n    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(chatUpdate.ContentUpdate))\n    {\n        System.Console.Write(chatUpdate.ContentUpdate);\n    }\n}\nSystem.Console.WriteLine(\"\");\n```\n\n\n\n\n## 5. Going beyond rate limits\n\nThe rate limits for the playground and free API usage are intended to help you experiment with models and prototype your AI application. For use beyond those limits, and to bring your application to scale, you must provision resources from an Azure account, and authenticate from there instead of your GitHub personal access token. You don't need to change anything else in your code. Use this link to [discover how to go beyond the free tier limits in Azure AI](https://ai.azure.com/github/model/meta-llama-3-8b-instruct).",
